{"Title":"An Act relative to discrimination against cash buyers","BillNumber":"H307","DocketNumber":"HD1588","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:49:42.247"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:49:42.2466667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H307/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 307) of Colleen M. Garry for legislation to require that all establishments be required to accept cash for transactions.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 10A of chapter 255D of the General Laws is hereby amended by at the end thereof, the following words: \"No retail or service establishment of any kind shall require the transfer of cash into electronic debit or credit cards to process transactions. All establishments shall be required to accept cash for any transaction.\"\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}